  "notes": "Load measured on a telemeterised vertebral body replacement (modified Synex, 6 load components, accuracy ~2% force / 5% moment of 3000 N / 20 Nm calibration range) that shares the load with the posterior internal fixator, residual vertebral bone and bone graft; the VBR force is NOT the total spinal load. Database search: for each patient the 10 exercises with the highest absolute difference from the supine preload value were identified, then pooled over patients to the overall top-10. Values are the patient maxima over all trials and sessions (few days - 65 months post-op), exercises performed in the patient's own way; large intra/inter-individual variation. Italic (not in that patient's own top 10) and bold (peak over patients) formatting is noted per row where read. Text: highest posterior shear ~230 N (printed -231 N) for arm elevation with weight in hands; posterior shear usually larger than anterior; VBR sagittal inclination ~10/5/0/2/1 deg (WP1-WP5)."
 },
